From d873cd8fdc4a3598e2466b7daa5b194a53f80585 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Stosse <1315-Harvester57@users.noreply.git.frama-c.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:43:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [e-acsl] read real constants with an exponent or in
 hexadecimal

A real constant that is not exactly a double is given to GMP as a
fraction, and Gmp.Q.normalize_str only converted plain decimal
expansions:

- with an exponent (1e-9) or in hexadecimal notation, the conversion
  raised Not_a_decimal, which nothing caught since the handler was
  left on Invalid_argument: Frama-C stopped on an unexpected error;
- with a suffix, that is for a long double constant such as 0.1L, the
  text was passed unchanged to __gmpq_set_str, which rejects it and
  leaves 0: "0.1L > 0.05" failed at run time and "0.1L == 0" held.

Exponent and hexadecimal notations are now converted with Zarith's
Q.of_string, which reads both exactly. A constant that still has its
suffix is reported as not yet supported, since its value depends on
the long double format of the target.

New test: arith/real_constants.c.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
